#{[17592186259651 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259651 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124282" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259651 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259651 #edb/ref 1071 "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u-v+1,\\,y=9u-4v+3.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=y-4x+a,\\,v=by+cx+3,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259651 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ab7706f1-5139-5e95-9482-c097bef51185" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259651 #edb/ref 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v+1 \\\\ 9u-4v+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ 9u-4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-4\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 9}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x-1 \\\\ y-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4\\cdot (x-1)+1\\cdot (y-3) \\\\ -9\\cdot (x-1)+2\\cdot (y-3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}y-4x+1 \\\\ 2y-9x+3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=y-4x+1,\\,v=2y+(-9)x+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+2+(-9)=-6.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259660 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259660 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124315" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259660 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259660 #edb/ref 1071 "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=5u-9v-2,\\,y=4u-8v+4.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=ax-\\frac{9}{4}y+b,\\,v=cx-\\frac{5}{4}y+7.\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259660 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2c660cc6-fa1c-504a-b604-d474fb35da3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259660 #edb/ref 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-9v-2 \\\\ 4u-8v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-9v \\\\ 4u-8v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -9 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-8\\cdot 5-(-9)\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-4}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x+2 \\\\ y-4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot (x+2)-\\frac{9}{4}\\cdot (y-4) \\\\ 1\\cdot (x+2)+(-\\frac{5}{4})\\cdot (y-4)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{9}{4}y+13 \\\\ x-\\frac{5}{4}y+7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=2x-\\frac{9}{4}y+13,\\,v=1x-\\frac{5}{4}y+7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+13+1=16.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278836 #edb/ref 1080 "A parallelepiped" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278836 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278836 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1acc367e-71f3-5e97-87ce-92842c5b3257" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279153 #edb/ref 1080 "A parallelogram" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279153 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279153 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3f4b22b4-65fa-5db1-94f1-780f0591f6e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279170 #edb/ref 1080 "A tetrahedron" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279170 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279170 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "411cf09f-aaa8-5213-a15d-e483b24650c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279497 #edb/ref 1080 "A line segment" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279497 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279497 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "638bcae2-f573-5b91-97f0-f5ab7fc66eb9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279720 #edb/ref 1080 "A point on the plane" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279720 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279720 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7e024141-a94e-5f97-ae2f-a04b85d857ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279807 #edb/ref 1080 "A triangle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279807 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279807 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "87fc0aa9-2d9d-5344-8ce5-d4d954e92fb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279951 #edb/ref 1080 "A point" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279951 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279951 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "99cffdbb-a38c-5a63-9d04-87167a638bb7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280049 #edb/ref 1080 "A triangle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280049 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280049 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a42ad425-777b-5f11-8db0-c06039f852ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280479 #edb/ref 1080 "A quadrilateral" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280479 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280479 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d5f74625-2c51-5fb6-83b9-61fbae0292bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280613 #edb/ref 1080 "A line segment" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280613 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280613 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e51121c0-fae9-532e-b1aa-79a388ca1f2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280888 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280888 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280888 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280888 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280888 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280888 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280888 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280888 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186279497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280888 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2222be89-5b86-5d7e-873f-1d11313d8d91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281132 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281132 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281132 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281132 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281132 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281132 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281132 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281132 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186279807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281132 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "aec2e96d-de39-5f66-aab1-77904959b9e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389257 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186389258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389257 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162215" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389257 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389257 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1f/1f550963f047a3860566564abc2cb1e9f3939125895912762ff751767ca55c57.png)\n\nConsider the affine transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nx=2u-v,\\,y=4u-v+2.\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the pentagon shown above under the action of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389257 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b31d6cdc-6f82-507f-838b-9eddf7b3f11a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389257 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that for any affine transformation \n\n$$\nT:u⟶Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $u$ and $b$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors, we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., when $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., when $det(A)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $A$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $A$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a point on the plane.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nThe given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ 4u-v+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ 4u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a non-singular matrix. \n\nTherefore, $T$ is invertible, and the image of the pentagon under the action of $T$ is a pentagon." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389258 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389258 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389258 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389258 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389258 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389258 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389258 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389258 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186389262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389258 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d1250926-eea3-55ee-b530-0094a4347a99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389259 #edb/ref 1080 "A square" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389259 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389259 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e04b870d-e25b-5d96-b606-28a110148002" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389260 #edb/ref 1080 "A point" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389260 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389260 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "062427a9-0f48-53fc-94f1-c6c3d5e866d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389261 #edb/ref 1080 "A triangle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389261 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389261 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b7b5ad5a-830d-59fb-be20-4b48087915f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389262 #edb/ref 1080 "A pentagon" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389262 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389262 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4003098a-783e-5e93-bb25-5f94f36652a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389263 #edb/ref 1080 "A line segment" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389263 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389263 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1f7e5e40-3f3f-5c2d-abac-4a9137d31956" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1045 "The Inverse of an Af